{title: Hosanna, Loud Hosanna}
{artist: Jennette Threlfall}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
Ho[F]sanna, loud ho[Bb]sanna, the [C]little children [F]sang;
through pillared court and [Bb]temple the [C]lovely anthem [F]rang.
To [Dm]Jesus, who had [Bb]blessed them close [F]folded to his [C]breast,
the [F]children sang their [Bb]praises, the [C]simplest and the [F]best.

Verse 2
From Olivet they followed [C]mid an [F]exultant
crowd, The victor palm [Bb]branch waving, [C]and chanting [F]clear
and [Dm]loud. The Lord [Bb]of men and angels [F]rode on in [C]lowly
state, [F]Nor scorned that [Bb]little children should [C]on His bidding [F]wait.

Verse 3
"Hosanna in the highest!" [C]that ancient [F]song
we sing, For Christ [Bb]is our [C]Redeemer, the [F]Lord
of [Dm]heav'n our King. [Bb]O may we ever [F]praise Him with [C]heart
and [F]life and voice, [Bb]And in His [C]blissful presence eternally [F]rejoice!
